

---

## 🔐 IRSA, Trust Policy & OIDC — Rapid Fire Interview Q&A
| #️⃣    | ❓ Question                                              | ✅ Answer                                                                                                                    |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1️⃣    | 🔐 What is a Trust Policy?                              | 👉 Defines who can assume an IAM role                                                                                       |
| 2️⃣    | 🎯 What does a Trust Policy control?                    | 👉 Who can access/assume the role                                                                                           |
| 3️⃣    | 📦 Which IAM entity contains Trust Policy?              | 👉 IAM Role                                                                                                                 |
| 4️⃣    | 📝 One-line definition of Trust Policy?                 | 👉 Defines trusted entities allowed to assume a role                                                                        |
| 5️⃣    | 👥 Common trusted entities in Trust Policy?             | 👉 IAM users, AWS services, AWS accounts, OIDC providers                                                                    |
| 6️⃣    | 🔄 What is `sts:AssumeRole`?                            | 👉 Assume role using AWS identity                                                                                           |
| 7️⃣    | 🌐 What is `sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`?             | 👉 Assume role using OIDC/JWT token                                                                                         |
| 8️⃣    | ☸️ Which STS action is used by IRSA?                    | 👉 `sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`                                                                                          |
| 9️⃣    | 🤔 Why does IRSA use AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity?         | 👉 Kubernetes provides OIDC tokens instead of AWS credentials                                                               |
| 🔟     | 🛡️ What is STS?                                        | 👉 AWS Security Token Service                                                                                               |
| 1️⃣1️⃣ | ⏳ Purpose of AWS STS?                                   | 👉 Generates temporary credentials                                                                                          |
| 1️⃣2️⃣ | ⚖️ Trust Policy vs Permission Policy?                   | 👉 Trust Policy = who can assume role; Permission Policy = allowed actions                                                  |
| 1️⃣3️⃣ | 🔑 Which policy defines AWS actions?                    | 👉 Permission Policy                                                                                                        |
| 1️⃣4️⃣ | 👤 Which policy defines trusted entities?               | 👉 Trust Policy                                                                                                             |
| 1️⃣5️⃣ | 📌 Where is Permission Policy attached?                 | 👉 User, Role, or Group                                                                                                     |
| 1️⃣6️⃣ | 📍 Where is Trust Policy attached?                      | 👉 IAM Role only                                                                                                            |
| 1️⃣7️⃣ | 👥 What is Principal in Trust Policy?                   | 👉 Trusted entity allowed to assume role                                                                                    |
| 1️⃣8️⃣ | ☁️ Example Principal for EC2?                           | 👉 `"ec2.amazonaws.com"`                                                                                                    |
| 1️⃣9️⃣ | ☸️ Example Principal for IRSA?                          | 👉 OIDC provider ARN                                                                                                        |
| 2️⃣0️⃣ | ⚙️ What is Effect field?                                | 👉 Allow or Deny access                                                                                                     |
| 2️⃣1️⃣ | ✅ Most common Effect value?                             | 👉 `"Allow"`                                                                                                                |
| 2️⃣2️⃣ | 🔒 Purpose of Condition in Trust Policy?                | 👉 Adds extra security restrictions                                                                                         |
| 2️⃣3️⃣ | 🛡️ Why is Condition important?                         | 👉 Prevents unauthorized role assumption                                                                                    |
| 2️⃣4️⃣ | 📋 Examples of Condition checks?                        | 👉 IP restriction, MFA, OIDC sub, aud claim                                                                                 |
| 2️⃣5️⃣ | 🌐 What is OIDC?                                        | 👉 OpenID Connect identity provider                                                                                         |
| 2️⃣6️⃣ | ☸️ Why is OIDC used in EKS?                             | 👉 Securely verifies Pod identities                                                                                         |
| 2️⃣7️⃣ | 🔑 What does OIDC provider do in IRSA?                  | 👉 AWS trusts Kubernetes-issued tokens                                                                                      |
| 2️⃣8️⃣ | ❌ What happens if OIDC provider is missing?             | 👉 IRSA fails completely                                                                                                    |
| 2️⃣9️⃣ | 🔍 Command to verify EKS OIDC provider?                 | 👉 `aws eks describe-cluster --name my-cluster --query "cluster.identity.oidc.issuer"`                                      |
| 3️⃣0️⃣ | 🔗 Command to enable OIDC provider?                     | 👉 `eksctl utils associate-iam-oidc-provider --cluster my-cluster --approve`                                                |
| 3️⃣1️⃣ | ☸️ What is IRSA?                                        | 👉 IAM Roles for Service Accounts                                                                                           |
| 3️⃣2️⃣ | 🎯 Main purpose of IRSA?                                | 👉 Secure AWS access for Pods without static credentials                                                                    |
| 3️⃣3️⃣ | 🚫 Problem solved by IRSA?                              | 👉 Avoid storing AWS keys inside Pods                                                                                       |
| 3️⃣4️⃣ | 📝 One-line IRSA definition?                            | 👉 Kubernetes Pods securely access AWS using IAM roles and OIDC                                                             |
| 3️⃣5️⃣ | 🔄 Core IRSA flow?                                      | 👉 Pod → ServiceAccount → IAM Role → AWS Access                                                                             |
| 3️⃣6️⃣ | 🔐 What does IRSA Trust Policy define?                  | 👉 Which Kubernetes ServiceAccount can assume IAM role                                                                      |
| 3️⃣7️⃣ | ⚡ Important action in IRSA Trust Policy?                | 👉 `"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"`                                                                                        |
| 3️⃣8️⃣ | 👤 What does `sub` condition represent?                 | 👉 Kubernetes ServiceAccount identity                                                                                       |
| 3️⃣9️⃣ | 🏷️ Format of IRSA `sub` value?                         | 👉 `system:serviceaccount:<namespace>:<serviceaccount>`                                                                     |
| 4️⃣0️⃣ | 📌 Example `sub` value?                                 | 👉 `system:serviceaccount:default:my-app`                                                                                   |
| 4️⃣1️⃣ | 📂 What does namespace in `sub` provide?                | 👉 Scope restriction                                                                                                        |
| 4️⃣2️⃣ | ❌ What happens if namespace mismatches?                 | 👉 Access denied                                                                                                            |
| 4️⃣3️⃣ | 🎯 Why add `aud: sts.amazonaws.com`?                    | 👉 Ensure token intended for AWS STS                                                                                        |
| 4️⃣4️⃣ | 🚫 What happens if `aud` missing?                       | 👉 Token validation fails                                                                                                   |
| 4️⃣5️⃣ | ⚠️ What happens if Condition removed from Trust Policy? | 👉 Any Pod could assume role                                                                                                |
| 4️⃣6️⃣ | ☠️ Why is wildcard `*` dangerous in Trust Policy?       | 👉 Allows excessive Pod access                                                                                              |
| 4️⃣7️⃣ | 📜 Command to create IAM policy?                        | 👉 `aws iam create-policy`                                                                                                  |
| 4️⃣8️⃣ | 🏗️ Command to create IAM role?                         | 👉 `aws iam create-role`                                                                                                    |
| 4️⃣9️⃣ | 🔗 Command to attach policy to role?                    | 👉 `aws iam attach-role-policy`                                                                                             |
| 5️⃣0️⃣ | 🛡️ Why attach least privilege policies?                | 👉 Minimize security risks                                                                                                  |
| 5️⃣1️⃣ | 👤 Purpose of Kubernetes ServiceAccount in IRSA?        | 👉 Pod identity                                                                                                             |
| 5️⃣2️⃣ | 🏷️ Important ServiceAccount annotation?                | 👉 `eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn`                                                                                             |
| 5️⃣3️⃣ | 🔗 What does annotation do?                             | 👉 Links IAM role to Kubernetes ServiceAccount                                                                              |
| 5️⃣4️⃣ | ❌ What happens if annotation is wrong?                  | 👉 Pod won’t get AWS access                                                                                                 |
| 5️⃣5️⃣ | 📥 Command to apply ServiceAccount YAML?                | 👉 `kubectl apply -f sa.yaml`                                                                                               |
| 5️⃣6️⃣ | 🔄 How does Pod get AWS credentials?                    | 👉 Pod calls STS using OIDC token                                                                                           |
| 5️⃣7️⃣ | 🔑 Are AWS access keys stored in Pod?                   | 👉 No                                                                                                                       |
| 5️⃣8️⃣ | ⏳ What type of credentials are returned?                | 👉 Temporary STS credentials                                                                                                |
| 5️⃣9️⃣ | 🔍 Command to verify identity inside Pod?               | 👉 `aws sts get-caller-identity`                                                                                            |
| 6️⃣0️⃣ | 📋 Expected output of get-caller-identity?              | 👉 IAM role ARN                                                                                                             |
| 6️⃣1️⃣ | 📂 Where is OIDC token mounted inside Pod?              | 👉 `/var/run/secrets/...`                                                                                                   |
| 6️⃣2️⃣ | 🔄 Does Kubernetes refresh OIDC token automatically?    | 👉 Yes                                                                                                                      |
| 6️⃣3️⃣ | 🔁 Internal IRSA authentication flow?                   | 👉 Pod starts → OIDC token mounted → STS AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity → Trust policy validation → Temporary credentials issued |
| 6️⃣4️⃣ | 🛡️ Who validates OIDC token?                           | 👉 AWS STS                                                                                                                  |
| 6️⃣5️⃣ | 🔍 What validates Pod identity?                         | 👉 Trust Policy `sub` condition                                                                                             |
| 6️⃣6️⃣ | ⚠️ Most common IRSA issue?                              | 👉 Namespace or ServiceAccount mismatch                                                                                     |
| 6️⃣7️⃣ | 🔎 IRSA not working — first thing to check?             | 👉 OIDC provider enabled                                                                                                    |
| 6️⃣8️⃣ | 👤 Pod using default ServiceAccount — why no access?    | 👉 Default SA usually has no IAM role annotation                                                                            |
| 6️⃣9️⃣ | 🔄 IRSA stopped after recreating EKS cluster — why?     | 👉 OIDC provider ID changed                                                                                                 |
| 7️⃣0️⃣ | 🛠️ Fix after OIDC ID changes?                          | 👉 Update Trust Policy                                                                                                      |
| 7️⃣1️⃣ | 👥 Multiple ServiceAccounts using same role — how?      | 👉 Use `StringLike` with multiple sub values                                                                                |
| 7️⃣2️⃣ | 🌍 Namespace-wide access example?                       | 👉 `system:serviceaccount:default:*`                                                                                        |
| 7️⃣3️⃣ | ⚠️ Is namespace-wide access recommended?                | 👉 No, avoid unless necessary                                                                                               |
| 7️⃣4️⃣ | 🛡️ Best IRSA security practice?                        | 👉 Least privilege                                                                                                          |
| 7️⃣5️⃣ | 🔒 Why separate IAM roles per app?                      | 👉 Reduce blast radius                                                                                                      |
| 7️⃣6️⃣ | ❌ Why avoid `Resource: "*"`?                            | 👉 Prevent over-permission                                                                                                  |
| 7️⃣7️⃣ | 📊 Why audit IAM roles regularly?                       | 👉 Detect misuse and privilege creep                                                                                        |
| 7️⃣8️⃣ | ☁️ EC2 accessing S3 uses what Principal?                | 👉 `ec2.amazonaws.com`                                                                                                      |
| 7️⃣9️⃣ | ☸️ EKS Pod accessing S3 securely uses what?             | 👉 IRSA                                                                                                                     |
| 8️⃣0️⃣ | 🔐 Why is IRSA better than access keys?                 | 👉 No static credentials                                                                                                    |
| 8️⃣1️⃣ | 🚀 Final one-line IRSA explanation?                     | 👉 OIDC + Trust Policy securely map Kubernetes Pods to IAM roles                                                            |
